# vim's Ctrl-D / Ctrl-U / Ctrl-F / Ctrl-B scroll the WINDOW and move the
# cursor the same number of lines (`:help CTRL-D`); before, only the
# cursor moved and the view followed once it ran off the bottom. The
# editor shows 36 rows here, so half a page is 18 lines and a page 34
# (the height less two). nvchad-probe, 38 rows: `gg<C-d>` top 20 cursor
# 20; `<C-d><C-d>` 39/39; `<C-f>` 37/37; `<C-f><C-b>` top 1 cursor 38;
# `5<C-d><C-d>` 11/11; `Gzz` top 82 of 100; `Gzt` top 100; `Gzb` top 63.
# Rows are read off the screen: `L00018` is line 18's text.
